{"content_hash": "326b5199c508bb95", "version_id": 745, "article_id": 75, "level_code": "en_c1", "lang": "en", "level": 5, "level_label": "C1 高级", "title": "Mob of 50 beats foreigner to death in Durban", "title_zh": "德班50人暴民围殴外籍男子致死", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck5yn9z3vnego?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1623438744990-f47414813a29?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Nnx8Y3Jvd2QlMjBiZWF0cyUyMGZvcmVpZ25lcnxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkyNzEzOTg0fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Amir Arabshahi on Unsplash", "author": "Amir Arabshahi", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@amir_arabshahi?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-crowd-of-people-with-their-hands-in-the-air-ERSKz8OrZIQ?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(69, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(107, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "d8d50814b11f"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-23", "word_count": 277, "reading_minutes": 1.4, "lead": "A foreign national has been killed by a crowd of around 50 people in the South African city of Durban, police say. The murder comes amid a wave of anti-immigrant protests that have turned violent this year.", "lead_zh": "南非警方称，一名外籍男子在德班市被约50人围殴致死。这起谋杀案发生之际，今年南非的反移民抗议浪潮已多次演变为暴力事件。", "preview": "According to police, the unidentified victim, believed to be in his late thirties or early forties, was initially approached by two men at t", "preview_zh": "据警方称，这名身份不明的受害者据信年近四十或四十出头，最初在路边被两名男子靠近，随后一大群人对他实施了袭击。他当场被宣告死亡，警方已立案调查，但作案动机尚未确定。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 733, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/75/en_c1.mp3", "duration": 109.2, "size_bytes": 656208, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 307, "has_timeline": true, "alternates": [{"voice": "af_bella", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/75/en_c1_af_bella.mp3", "duration": 112.275, "size_bytes": 674640, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 307, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/75/en_c1_af_bella.json"}, {"voice": "am_michael", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/75/en_c1_am_michael.mp3", "duration": 119.375, "size_bytes": 717264, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 307, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/75/en_c1_am_michael.json"}, {"voice": "bf_emma", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/75/en_c1_bf_emma.mp3", "duration": 102.325, "size_bytes": 614880, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 307, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/75/en_c1_bf_emma.json"}, {"voice": "bm_george", "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/75/en_c1_bm_george.mp3", "duration": 112.975, "size_bytes": 678816, "engine": "kokoro", "word_count": 307, "has_timeline": true, "timeline_url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/timeline/75/en_c1_bm_george.json"}]}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@79c5bce/content/data/versions/745.json", "paragraphs": ["According to police, the unidentified victim, believed to be in his late thirties or early forties, was initially approached by two men at the roadside before a larger group set upon him. He was pronounced dead at the scene, and an investigation has been opened, though the motive has yet to be established.", "The killing follows a series of protests targeting immigrants across South Africa this year, some of which have descended into violence. Earlier this month, shops and cars were set alight in Durban and in Soweto, near Johannesburg, prompting the government to urge demonstrators to act peacefully while conceding that immigration reforms are needed.", "Provincial police spokesperson Robert Netshiunda told the BBC that officers could not speculate on the motive and would share further details once verified. One of the groups behind the protests, March and March, had initially set a 30 June deadline for all undocumented migrants to leave the country, and several demonstrations were held ahead of it.", "Reports of attacks on people from other African countries prompted Zimbabwe, Nigeria and Ghana to repatriate citizens amid fears of further violence. Nigeria accused South African authorities of responsibility for the deaths of two of its nationals that month, while Ghana confirmed that a citizen, Bashiru Isak, was fatally shot in Cape Town.", "South Africa has grappled with xenophobic attacks for nearly two decades; in 2008, more than 60 people were killed and tens of thousands displaced. The latest unrest unfolds against a backdrop of widespread poverty, deep inequality and unemployment affecting roughly a third of the workforce, though researchers say claims that migrants fuel crime and strain services are not borne out by evidence."], "paragraphs_zh": ["据警方称，这名身份不明的受害者据信年近四十或四十出头，最初在路边被两名男子靠近，随后一大群人对他实施了袭击。他当场被宣告死亡，警方已立案调查，但作案动机尚未确定。", "这起命案发生之前，南非今年已出现一系列针对移民的抗议活动，其中一些演变为暴力事件。本月早些时候，德班和约翰内斯堡附近的索韦托有商店和汽车被纵火焚烧，政府随后敦促示威者和平行事，同时承认有必要进行移民改革。", "省警方发言人罗伯特·内齐温达告诉BBC，警方无法推测作案动机，待核实后将公布更多细节。抗议活动背后的组织之一“三月又三月”最初要求所有无证移民在6月30日前离开南非，该期限之前已举行过数场示威。", "针对其他非洲国家侨民的袭击报道，促使津巴布韦、尼日利亚和加纳出于对进一步暴力的担忧而安排本国公民回国。尼日利亚指责南非当局应对当月两名本国公民的死亡负责，加纳则证实本国公民巴希鲁·伊萨克在开普敦被枪杀。", "近二十年来，南非一直难以摆脱排外袭击的阴影；2008年，大规模针对外籍人士的袭击造成60多人死亡、数万人流离失所。最新一轮动荡的背景是普遍贫困、严重不平等以及影响约三分之一劳动力的失业问题，尽管研究人员表示，有关移民推高犯罪、挤占公共服务的说法并无证据支持。"], "body": "According to police, the unidentified victim, believed to be in his late thirties or early forties, was initially approached by two men at the roadside before a larger group set upon him. He was pronounced dead at the scene, and an investigation has been opened, though the motive has yet to be established.\n\nThe killing follows a series of protests targeting immigrants across South Africa this year, some of which have descended into violence. Earlier this month, shops and cars were set alight in Durban and in Soweto, near Johannesburg, prompting the government to urge demonstrators to act peacefully while conceding that immigration reforms are needed.\n\nProvincial police spokesperson Robert Netshiunda told the BBC that officers could not speculate on the motive and would share further details once verified. One of the groups behind the protests, March and March, had initially set a 30 June deadline for all undocumented migrants to leave the country, and several demonstrations were held ahead of it.\n\nReports of attacks on people from other African countries prompted Zimbabwe, Nigeria and Ghana to repatriate citizens amid fears of further violence. Nigeria accused South African authorities of responsibility for the deaths of two of its nationals that month, while Ghana confirmed that a citizen, Bashiru Isak, was fatally shot in Cape Town.\n\nSouth Africa has grappled with xenophobic attacks for nearly two decades; in 2008, more than 60 people were killed and tens of thousands displaced. The latest unrest unfolds against a backdrop of widespread poverty, deep inequality and unemployment affecting roughly a third of the workforce, though researchers say claims that migrants fuel crime and strain services are not borne out by evidence.", "body_zh": "据警方称，这名身份不明的受害者据信年近四十或四十出头，最初在路边被两名男子靠近，随后一大群人对他实施了袭击。他当场被宣告死亡，警方已立案调查，但作案动机尚未确定。\n\n这起命案发生之前，南非今年已出现一系列针对移民的抗议活动，其中一些演变为暴力事件。本月早些时候，德班和约翰内斯堡附近的索韦托有商店和汽车被纵火焚烧，政府随后敦促示威者和平行事，同时承认有必要进行移民改革。\n\n省警方发言人罗伯特·内齐温达告诉BBC，警方无法推测作案动机，待核实后将公布更多细节。抗议活动背后的组织之一“三月又三月”最初要求所有无证移民在6月30日前离开南非，该期限之前已举行过数场示威。\n\n针对其他非洲国家侨民的袭击报道，促使津巴布韦、尼日利亚和加纳出于对进一步暴力的担忧而安排本国公民回国。尼日利亚指责南非当局应对当月两名本国公民的死亡负责，加纳则证实本国公民巴希鲁·伊萨克在开普敦被枪杀。\n\n近二十年来，南非一直难以摆脱排外袭击的阴影；2008年，大规模针对外籍人士的袭击造成60多人死亡、数万人流离失所。最新一轮动荡的背景是普遍贫困、严重不平等以及影响约三分之一劳动力的失业问题，尽管研究人员表示，有关移民推高犯罪、挤占公共服务的说法并无证据支持。", "text": "According to police, the unidentified victim, believed to be in his late thirties or early forties, was initially approached by two men at the roadside before a larger group set upon him. He was pronounced dead at the scene, and an investigation has been opened, though the motive has yet to be established. The killing follows a series of protests targeting immigrants across South Africa this year, some of which have descended into violence. Earlier this month, shops and cars were set alight in Durban and in Soweto, near Johannesburg, prompting the government to urge demonstrators to act peacefully while conceding that immigration reforms are needed. Provincial police spokesperson Robert Netshiunda told the BBC that officers could not speculate on the motive and would share further details once verified. One of the groups behind the protests, March and March, had initially set a 30 June deadline for all undocumented migrants to leave the country, and several demonstrations were held ahead of it. Reports of attacks on people from other African countries prompted Zimbabwe, Nigeria and Ghana to repatriate citizens amid fears of further violence. Nigeria accused South African authorities of responsibility for the deaths of two of its nationals that month, while Ghana confirmed that a citizen, Bashiru Isak, was fatally shot in Cape Town. South Africa has grappled with xenophobic attacks for nearly two decades; in 2008, more than 60 people were killed and tens of thousands displaced. The latest unrest unfolds against a backdrop of widespread poverty, deep inequality and unemployment affecting roughly a third of the workforce, though researchers say claims that migrants fuel crime and strain services are not borne out by evidence.", "vocab": [{"word": "set upon", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "袭击；围攻", "note": "正式用语，常见于新闻报道，指一群人突然攻击某人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "pronounced dead", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "被宣告死亡", "note": "警方或医疗新闻固定搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "speculate", "pos": "verb", "zh": "推测；猜测", "note": "常与 on/about 连用，警方常用 cannot speculate on the motive", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "descend into", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "陷入（混乱、暴力等）", "note": "descend into violence/chaos，书面语", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "set alight", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "点燃；纵火焚烧", "note": "比 set fire to 更书面", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "concede", "pos": "verb", "zh": "承认（常指不情愿地）", "note": "后接 that 从句，政治新闻高频", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "repatriate", "pos": "verb", "zh": "遣返；使回国", "note": "名词形式 repatriation", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "undocumented migrant", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "无证移民", "note": "中性正式说法，避免用 illegal immigrant", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "grapple with", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "努力应对；设法解决", "note": "grapple with a problem/issue", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "xenophobic", "pos": "adj", "zh": "排外的；仇外的", "note": "名词 xenophobia，报道移民议题常用", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "displaced", "pos": "adj", "zh": "流离失所的", "note": "常与 tens of thousands 等数量词搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "backdrop", "pos": "noun", "zh": "背景", "note": "against a backdrop of... 固定搭配", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "borne out", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "得到证实", "note": "bear out 的过去分词，常用 be borne out by evidence", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "strain", "pos": "verb", "zh": "使承受压力；使紧张", "note": "strain public services 给公共服务带来压力", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Crowd of 50 beats foreigner to death in South Africa", "summary_original": "The attack on the unidentified victim follows a wave of anti-migrants protests in South Africa this year.", "body_original": "Crowd of 50 beats foreigner to death in South Africa\nBy\nOndiro Oganga\nPublished\n7 hours ago\nA foreign national has been beaten to death by a crowd of about 50 people in Durban, South Africa, police say.\nAccording to police, the unidentified man, believed to be in his late 30s or early 40s, was first approached by two men by the roadside before being assaulted by a larger group. He was pronounced dead at the scene.\nPolice have launched an investigation into the murder, with the motive yet to be established.\nThe killing follows a wave of protests against immigrants in South Africa this year, some of which have turned violent. Earlier this month, shops and cars were set on fire in Durban, as well as Soweto, near Johannesburg.\nProvincial police spokesperson Robert Netshiunda told the BBC they cannot speculate on the motive for the killing in Durban and that more information would be shared once verified.\n'We have to prioritise South Africans': Anti-migrant movement blocks foreigners from healthcare\nPublished\n18 October 2025\nThe uniformed group targeting foreigners in South Africa\nPublished\n18 September 2023\nThe government has urged the demonstrators to act peacefully, while also accepting the need for immigration reforms. It says tens of thousands of foreign nationals have been deported or repatriated since it launched a crackdown earlier this year.\nOne of the groups behind the protests, March and March, had initially set a deadline of 30 June for all undocumented migrants to leave South Africa.\nSeveral protests were held ahead of that deadline, with reports of attacks on people from other African countries.\nThese prompted several countries, including Zimbabwe, Nigeria and Ghana, to take steps to repatriate their citizens amid fears of further violence.\nNigeria accused South African authorities of responsibility for the deaths of two of its citizens that month.\nGhana also confirmed the death of a citizen, Bashiru Isak, a father of three who was fatally shot in Cape Town during demonstrations targeting foreign nationals.\nHis death led to a diplomatic row with South Africa, which said the scale of the violence had been exaggerated.\nOne of the leaders of the March and March movement, Jacinta Ngobese-Zuma, denied that she was xenophobic.\n\"We can't be living with these people for so many years and now when we say it is too much, it is enough, we are told that we are xenophobic,\" she told the BBC's Focus on Africa programme.\nSouth Africa has struggled with xenophobic attacks for nearly two decades. In 2008, more than 60 people were killed and tens of thousands displaced during widespread attacks on foreign nationals.\nThe latest unrest comes against a backdrop of widespread poverty, deep inequality and unemployment affecting roughly a third of the workforce.\nMigrants are frequently accused of taking jobs, contributing to crime and placing pressure on public services, although researchers say such sweeping claims are not supported by evidence.\nDespite its economic difficulties, South Africa remains one of the continent's main destinations for migrants seeking employment, safety and better opportunities.\nAdditional reporting by Pumza Fihlani in Johannesburg\nMore from South Africa on the BBC:\n'They came with machetes' - deadline looms for migrants to leave South Africa\nPublished\n17 June\nThe king's speech - and why it has foreigners in South Africa worried\nPublished\n1 February\nGo to\nBBCAfrica.com\n,\nexternal\nfor more news from the African continent.\nFollow us on Twitter\n@BBCAfrica\n,\nexternal\n, on Facebook at\nBBC Africa\n,\nexternal\nor on Instagram at\nbbcafrica\n,\nexternal\nRelated topics\nAfrica\nMigration\nSouth Africa\nDurban\nBBC Africa podcasts\nFocus on Africa\nThis Is Africa", "fetched_at": "2026-10-23T00:06:23.045368", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "According", "s": 0.275, "e": 0.65, "sm": 275, "em": 650, "cs": 0, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "to", "s": 0.65, "e": 0.75, "sm": 650, "em": 749, "cs": 10, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "police", "s": 0.75, "e": 1.475, "sm": 750, "em": 1475, "cs": 13, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": ",", "s": 1.475, "e": 1.575, "sm": 1475, "em": 1574, "cs": 19, "ce": 20, "s